# Environment post-processors, run before any bean exists.
#
# HostDatabaseEnvironmentPostProcessor derives DB_URL / DB_USERNAME / DB_PASSWORD from a
# managed PostgreSQL's own variables (DATABASE_URL, or PGHOST/PGPORT/PGDATABASE/PGUSER/
# PGPASSWORD) for whichever of them is not set directly.
#
# RequiredEnvironmentPostProcessor then refuses to start on a deployed server (the staging,
# prod or atmos profile) with any required setting missing, naming all of them at once.
#
# Both run last (Ordered.LOWEST_PRECEDENCE and one before it), so application.yaml, any
# .env and the active profiles have already been read.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
uz.minipolya.minipolya_backend.config.env.HostDatabaseEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
uz.minipolya.minipolya_backend.config.env.RequiredEnvironmentPostProcessor
